<p class="lt-chem-127561">Acquiring samples over an extended period of time introduces a substantial time-dependent change in the concentration of monensin. Because the variation in concentration between samples is so large, we use a paired <em>t</em>-test with the following null and alternative hypotheses.</p>

<p class="lt-chem-127561">\[H_0 \text{: } \overline{d} = 0 \quad \quad \quad H_A \text{: } \overline{d} \neq 0 \nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-127561">Defining the difference between the methods as</p>

<p class="lt-chem-127561">\[d_i = (X_\text{elect})_i - (X_\text{micro})_i \nonumber\]</p>

